uid "61124a49-e750-5eed-9f63-4fab70f48c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\pi n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398580} {:answer/id #uuid "282a04d7-5121-553a-8c70-66602f8c83db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398581} {:answer/id #uuid "4a1c8270-8fd2-50fc-8447-30acc60e9312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398582}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398578} :answer-field/id #uuid "4112b8f8-a1d3-5ca1-a272-50f00bc81e5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b2987e81-f85b-5262-9ea2-835ea44d86e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162644" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(t+1)\\,i+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)\\,j+{e}^{-t}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\bbox[5pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $t+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n3t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."} :step/id #uuid "3ce5a87f-f4ad-59bf-8bf7-3a76cd4d166e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411594}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411592 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281524 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d759664-71cf-5524-8292-b4f9f56698b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t\\in (-1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279292} {:answer/id #uuid "839d4983-b3e1-5df2-929b-e864ccf4fcda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t\\in (-1,0)\\cup (0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279769} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed76513-0186-5831-b557-a4f08af7383f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t\\in (-1,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279863} {:answer/id #uuid "ad393dc1-dc55-547e-b037-d30e59fc192b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t\\in (0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280126} {:answer/id #uuid "b43b6b14-c660-5371-ab23-f23367846209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t\\in [0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280178}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280126} :answer-field/id #uuid "685912e0-327e-5f2f-962f-61ee3eb96008" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0b92442b-8b2c-57b7-8241-452f363996f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-162662" :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{t}$ is $t\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)$ is $s\\in (-1,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\frac{1}{t}$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/97/971a65619088884002784f5abb3c4f3dc9b2e17e6b905f171b8106219a139557.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (0,\\infty ).$"} :step/id #uuid "3f69fac6-c791-5076-b0cb-1df861e3f01d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411593}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411593 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363458 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b740762-045e-5820-a736-1fe5651b59de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "s\\in (-2,0)\\cup (0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363460} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f05f0a-6614-5d5d-9df5-da7e78375081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "s\\in (-2,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363461} {:answer/id #uuid "43be1e1f-d373-53b1-afef-1ef4c39e04b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "s\\in (-2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363462} {:answer/id #uuid "aef37efd-8619-5880-9e33-8cc7399e16db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "s\\in (-2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363463} {:answer/id #uuid "3bcc0512-6302-5ee0-b419-66a663e9083e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "s\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363464}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363463} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e9a1fab-e156-581f-bef9-19ac8957daa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7f5ab3ef-ae4b-58ea-a096-4f661af5c41f" :question/math-academy-id "q-162663" :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)=\\sqrt{1-s}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+2)\\,j+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-s)\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{1-s}$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,1].$\n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+2)$ is $s\\in (-2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-s)$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,0).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/6a/6a2d170c22a544335735e859dd080d74964a4d5b5053789a557b5ea406f9d3a9.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is $s\\in (-2,0).$"} :step/id #uuid "649a877d-0747-58ab-aefc-0fc49ca6326f"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411594 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281516 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5826ca19-6daa-5fae-a51f-ca9bd88aa67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\pi n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279403} {:answer/id #uuid "5f4eec8a-dc19-556b-aef1-89da49e75d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279466} {:answer/id #uuid "b0252ebd-3528-5293-87d9-bd4c3a5eac03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280152} {:answer/id #uuid "c2dc73e9-c351-5c0a-b627-1ba7b9ce1e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\pi n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280303} {:answer/id #uuid "d106d3f2-6dbf-539d-b0e1-363e4e8caf2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280434}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280152} :answer-field/id #uuid "e58ed6b3-82ba-5b40-8a75-2b63a00c7ed1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9d16926a-5957-5fb2-9fde-8f7ccb3e0a44" :question/math-academy-id "q-162650" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3t))\\,i+3t\\,j+(2-{t}^{2})\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n3t=\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $3t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $2-{t}^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."} :step/id #uuid "70d11093-23ab-55b7-88e4-81ad27b59786" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411592}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411595 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115510 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4e7ea98-c99e-5e1a-b0a7-704c7552fe2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363420} {:answer/id #uuid "516f0376-d461-50f1-9446-88d42e4dd246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363421} {:answer/id #uuid "606a6900-ad5d-54ed-92c9-7c9c48c4ff11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363422} {:answer/id #uuid "df8725b2-1bdf-5492-bb7d-22cf79b754fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363423} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b51453-7d1a-5d7d-92fc-c5d50c4ca073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363424}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363424} :answer-field/id #uuid "669d7279-38d4-5150-94a0-6a97a679c0f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b7cf4d71-17d1-5d39-bf9c-739bde65f8a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160767" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$, $t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."} :step/id #uuid "afc5168b-5251-58d8-8fc1-8965074ea6cd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411591}}] :activity/title "The Domain of a Vector-Valued Function" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411590}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420096} :activity/id #uuid "d63840d2-3609-5c32-bdc9-4fe9ce0a42cd" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049186 :topic/id #uuid "e1c10e80-3811-5fcd-98a3-8118c49347e4" :topic/math-academy-id 1737} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420094 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54811e57-5329-5901-9031-55945bdb3aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420082} {:answer/id #uuid "656b42d3-126c-5abb-9880-9e0fc6a9e621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2\\pi n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420083} {:answer/id #uuid "6d5d9399-1eaf-57c4-b24e-dd